Description: Derive a unit's drop-in candidate names once, not once per lookup directory
 unit_file_find_dirs() ran once for every unit name or alias, lookup directory and drop-in
 suffix, and each call worked out the unit's candidate names again: the name, its template,
 its "-" prefixes. They depend on the name alone. Upstream computes them once per name and
 builds each path with one strjoin(). Its author measured manager_enumerate() 45.35 -> 38.81
 ms, 50 runs, ~270 units, PID 1 in a container, and `systemd --test` output byte-identical.
 .
 Backported to 259 unchanged but for the context of one removed line, where 259 calls
 set_get() and upstream set_contains().
 .
 Measured on spin-machine (docs/image.md, "The rebuilt packages"): the first SSH login
 -6.5 ms [-9.9, -1.3], 100 boots a side against systemd rebuilt without it; PID 1's CPU before
 the login 56.0 -> 52.4 ms, p50 of 5 (spin-stack/machine labs 45090299768, 45090326943).
Author: Eric Curtin <eric.curtin@docker.com>
Origin: backport, https://github.com/systemd/systemd/pull/42858
Applied-Upstream: v262
Last-Update: 2026-11-23

